+# hidden-state recurrence, and a digit-normalized "canonical template"
+# periodicity check built specifically to catch the repeated-bisection-with-
+# different-literals shape this investigation's own rambling case actually
+# has) ALL fail to reliably separate productive from unproductive
+# generation -- the canonical-template check in particular fires heavily
+# and early (16% through, 100+ times) on a case that succeeds, while never
+# firing at all on the case it was built to catch, once tuned to avoid
+# false-positiving on ordinary piecewise-case enumeration; (3) the one
+# signal that DID show a strong, real correlation all session is the
+# model's OWN self-report -- runs containing a spontaneous "this is
+# messy"/"I'm stuck"-type phrase run ~2.7x longer and hit the token cap
+# ~6.5x more often than runs without one, checked across the full AIME24
+# corpus (see analysis/semantic_guard/README.md).
